From: restomod bluewhale bring-up, 2026-11-16
Subject: [PATCH] deepseek_v4: import deep_gemm at the call site, not at module scope

``mhc_mega.py`` imported ``deep_gemm`` at module scope behind ``if is_cuda()``,
and ``deepseek_v4_mhc`` imports ``mhc_mega`` at module scope, so the whole
DeepSeek-V4 model class is unimportable on any host without DeepGEMM.

The kernel is only reached when ``_can_use_mega_mhc`` is true, and that
requires sm100, so on sm70 the import is the only thing that ever runs: the
registry skipped the model, fell back to the generic HF wrapper, and the load
died with ``Unrecognized configuration class DeepseekV41Config`` -- a config
error naming the wrong file. Moving the import into the function makes the
model class importable on V100 and never enters the sm100 path.

Verified: ``import sglang.srt.models.deepseek_v4`` succeeds on V100 with this
patch and fails without it; ``EntryClass = [DeepseekV4ForCausalLM]`` registers.

---
--- a/python/sglang/kernels/ops/layernorm/mhc_mega.py
+++ b/python/sglang/kernels/ops/layernorm/mhc_mega.py
@@ -5,11 +5,6 @@
 """
 
 import torch
-
-from sglang.srt.utils import is_cuda
-
-if is_cuda():
-    import deep_gemm
 
 
 def mhc_mega_boundary(
@@ -38,6 +33,12 @@
     on the capture stream to initialize DeepGEMM's per-stream barriers.
     ``y_fp8`` / ``y_gemm_sf`` also receive the normed rows as a DeepGEMM MXFP8 pair.
     """
+    # DeepGEMM ships Hopper/Blackwell kernels only, but this module is imported
+    # by the DeepSeek-V4 model chain on every platform. Import it where the
+    # kernel is called: ``_can_use_mega_mhc`` already restricts the call to
+    # sm100, so on sm70 the module imports and this function never runs.
+    import deep_gemm
+
     rows, hidden = x.shape
     hc = residual.shape[1]
     updated = torch.empty_like(residual)
